<title>INDIA: Hundreds of trucks stranded at Indo-Nepali border.</title>
<headline>Hundreds of trucks stranded at Indo-Nepali border.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-12-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hundreds of trucks were lined up in India waiting to enter Nepal on Sunday because border officials had not yet been informed of a bilateral trade agreement, the Press Trust of India (PTI) said.</p>
<p>The news agency said trucks carrying goods including petroleum products were stranded at Bahraich town on the border following the expiry of a bilateral trade treaty on Friday.</p>
<p>The treaty was extended for five years on Tuesday, but PTI said excise and customs officials had stopped all trucks from midnight on Friday as there had been no official confirmation of the deal. People were still allowed to cross the border.</p>
</text>
